# Core UI Package - Cursor AI Rules & Context

## Project Overview

This is **@core-erp/ui** - the centralized UI component library and design system for the Core ERP ecosystem. It provides shared components, utilities, and design tokens for the main Core ERP application and all plugins.

### Key Architecture Points

1. **Shared UI Package**: One package, used by main app and all plugins
2. **Peer Dependency Model**: Plugins use @core-erp/ui as peer dependency
3. **Design System**: Complete design tokens and component library
4. **Build Target**: Library (not application)

### Tech Stack

- **React 18**: Functional components with hooks
- **TypeScript 5**: Strict mode, full type safety
- **Tailwind CSS 3**: Utility-first styling with custom preset
- **Radix UI**: Accessible component primitives
- **Vite 5**: Fast build tool for library bundling
- **date-fns**: Date formatting and manipulation

### Package Structure

```
@core-erp/ui/
├── src/
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── ui/              # 48 shadcn/ui components
│   │   ├── responsive/      # 6 custom responsive components
│   │   └── loading/         # 2 skeleton loading components
│   ├── lib/                 # Utilities (cn, formatters)
│   ├── hooks/               # Custom React hooks
│   ├── styles/              # Global CSS and variables
│   └── types/               # TypeScript type definitions
├── dist/                    # Build output (gitignored)
├── docs/                    # Comprehensive documentation
├── tailwind.config.js       # Exportable Tailwind preset
└── package.json             # Package metadata with exports
```

## Component Inventory

### 48 shadcn/ui Components
Standard, accessible UI components:
- **Form Controls**: Button, Input, Textarea, Checkbox, Radio, Select, Switch, Slider, Calendar, Label, Form, InputOTP
- **Data Display**: Table, Card, Badge, Avatar, Tooltip, HoverCard, Popover, Accordion, Collapsible, Chart, Carousel, AspectRatio
- **Feedback**: Alert, AlertDialog, Dialog, Toast, Toaster, Progress, Skeleton, Drawer, Sheet
- **Navigation**: Breadcrumb, Tabs, NavigationMenu, Menubar, DropdownMenu, ContextMenu, Command, Pagination, Sidebar
- **Layout**: Separator, ScrollArea, Resizable, Toggle, ToggleGroup

### 6 Custom Responsive Components
- **PageContainer**: Responsive page wrapper with max-width control
- **PageHeader**: Consistent page headers with title, subtitle, actions
- **ResponsiveGrid**: Grid layout adapting to screen size
- **ResponsiveStack**: Vertical/horizontal stacks with responsive spacing
- **ResponsiveButton**: Button with responsive sizing
- **ResponsiveTable**: Mobile-friendly table with card fallback

### 2 Loading Components
- **SkeletonCard**: Card skeleton loader
- **SkeletonTable**: Table skeleton loader

### Utilities
- **cn()**: Class name merging with Tailwind conflict resolution
- **formatDate()**: Locale-aware date formatting
- **formatDateTime()**: Date and time formatting
- **formatRelativeTime()**: Relative time ("2 hours ago")
- **formatNumber()**: Number formatting with locale
- **formatCurrency()**: Currency formatting (USD, THB)
- **formatPercentage()**: Percentage formatting

### Hooks
- **useToast()**: Toast notification management (sonner)
- **useIsMobile()**: Responsive breakpoint detection

## Code Patterns to Follow

### 1. Component Structure

All UI components follow this pattern:

```typescript
import * as React from 'react'
import { cva, type VariantProps } from 'class-variance-authority'
import { cn } from '../../lib/utils'

// Define variants using cva
const componentVariants = cva(
  "base-classes",
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        default: "default-classes",
        secondary: "secondary-classes",
      },
      size: {
        default: "default-size",
        sm: "small-size",
        lg: "large-size",
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: "default",
      size: "default",
    },
  }
)

// Props interface extending HTML element
export interface ComponentProps
  extends React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLElement>,
    VariantProps<typeof componentVariants> {
  asChild?: boolean // For polymorphic components
}

// Component with forwardRef
const Component = React.forwardRef<HTMLElement, ComponentProps>(
  ({ className, variant, size, ...props }, ref) => {
    return (
      <element
        className={cn(componentVariants({ variant, size, className }))}
        ref={ref}
        {...props}
      />
    )
  }
)
Component.displayName = "Component"

export { Component, componentVariants }
```

### 2. Responsive Components

Custom responsive components use Tailwind breakpoints:

```typescript
import { cn } from '../../lib/utils'

interface ResponsiveComponentProps {
  // Required props
  title: string
  // Optional props
  subtitle?: string
  className?: string
}

export function ResponsiveComponent({ 
  title, 
  subtitle, 
  className 
}: ResponsiveComponentProps) {
  return (
    <div className={cn(
      // Mobile first
      'flex flex-col gap-2 p-4',
      // Tablet
      'md:flex-row md:items-center md:gap-4 md:p-6',
      // Desktop
      'lg:gap-6 lg:p-8',
      className
    )}>
      <h1 className="text-2xl md:text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-bold">
        {title}
      </h1>
      {subtitle && (
        <p className="text-sm md:text-base text-muted-foreground">
          {subtitle}
        </p>
      )}
    </div>
  )
}
```

### 3. Utility Functions

All utilities are pure functions with clear types:

```typescript
/**
 * Format a date with locale support
 * @param date - Date to format
 * @param locale - User's locale
 * @param formatStr - date-fns format string
 * @returns Formatted date string
 */
export function formatDate(
  date: Date | string,
  locale: SupportedLocale = 'en',
  formatStr: string = 'PP'
): string {
  try {
    const dateObj = typeof date === 'string' ? parseISO(date) : date
    return format(dateObj, formatStr, { locale: dateFnsLocales[locale] })
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error formatting date:', error)
    return String(date)
  }
}
```

### 4. Hooks

Custom hooks follow React conventions:

```typescript
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react'

export function useCustomHook(initialValue: string) {
  const [value, setValue] = useState(initialValue)
  
  useEffect(() => {
    // Side effects here
  }, [value])
  
  return { value, setValue }
}
```

